From: Daedal <daedal@localhost>
Date: Thu, 23 Jul 2026 17:22:00 -0700
Subject: [PATCH] KVM: x86/PVM: allow host-initiated MSR_IA32_FEAT_CTL writes

pvm_set_msr() rejects MSR_IA32_FEAT_CTL outright on non-Intel hosts
(`if (!is_intel || ...) return 1`). kvm-pvm nonetheless advertises the MSR
in KVM_GET_MSR_INDEX_LIST, so a VMM (Firecracker) that snapshots the full
supported-MSR set and replays it on restore issues KVM_SET_MSRS including
FEAT_CTL as a host-initiated write. On a non-Intel host (e.g. a qemu-TCG
"AMD" vCPU) the write is rejected, KVM_SET_MSRS returns a partial count, and
Firecracker's snapshot restore fails with:

  Failed to restore vCPUs: Failed to set all KVM MSRs for this vCPU.
  Only a partial write was done.

Mainline KVM validates such control MSRs only for guest-originated writes and
trusts host-initiated (VMM) writes. Gate the validity check on
!msr_info->host_initiated so snapshot restore succeeds while guest writes are
still validated. This makes PVM microVM live-migration work; without it the
base snapshot/boot succeed but every restore fails.

Signed-off-by: Daedal <daedal@localhost>
---
 arch/x86/kvm/pvm/pvm.c | 3 ++-
 1 file changed, 2 insertions(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/arch/x86/kvm/pvm/pvm.c b/arch/x86/kvm/pvm/pvm.c
index 71cf60159..8a1b2c3d4 100644
--- a/arch/x86/kvm/pvm/pvm.c
+++ b/arch/x86/kvm/pvm/pvm.c
@@ -1059,7 +1059,8 @@ static int pvm_set_msr(struct kvm_vcpu *vcpu, struct msr_data *msr_info)
 		/* It is ignored now. */
 		break;
 	case MSR_IA32_FEAT_CTL:
-		if (!is_intel || !is_pvm_feature_control_msr_valid(pvm, msr_info))
+		if (!msr_info->host_initiated &&
+		    (!is_intel || !is_pvm_feature_control_msr_valid(pvm, msr_info)))
 			return 1;
 		pvm->msr_ia32_feature_control = data;
 		break;
--
2.43.0
